meta {
  name: Ticket status
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/method/implementor.client_api.get_ticket?ticket=12hnuea73s
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ticket: 12hnuea73s
  ~customer: Hamza
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });
  
  test("has message", function () {
    expect(res.body).to.have.property("message");
  });

  test("has module, created and ratings", function () {
    expect(res.body.message).to.include.keys("module", "created", "ratings");
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Returns one ticket with its timeline, comments and attachments.
  
  **Endpoint:** `GET /api/method/implementor.client_api.get_ticket`  
  **Screen:** Ticket status
  
  **Permission:** Signed-in client user (Client User or Client Admin). Only records of the user's own client company are returned.
  
  **Query parameters:**
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Example | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `ticket` | string | yes | `12hnuea73s` | Ticket `name`. |
  | `customer` | string | no | `Hamza` | Not used by the app. The server picks the user's company. Disabled by default. |
  
  **Response (trimmed):**
  
  ```json
  {
    "message": {
      "name": "12h2sd9uia",
      "subject": "Stock valuation report is blank",
      "description": "Module: Stock\nScreen or document: Stock Ledger\n\nThe report shows no rows.",
      "project": "PROJ-0029",
      "project_title": "Hamza ERPNext Implementation",
      "module": "Stock",
      "ticket_type": "Bug",
      "priority": "Normal",
      "status": "Resolved",
      "raised_by": "Aisha Khan",
      "created": "2026-10-28 15:41:40.112233",
      "sla_due": "2026-10-30 15:41:40",
      "resolution_notes": "Valuation method was missing on the item group.",
      "assigned_to": ["Mohammed Ali"],
      "hours_logged": 2.5,
      "progress": 100,
      "steps": [
        { "status": "New", "at": "2026-10-28 15:41:40.112233", "done": true, "current": false },
        { "status": "Triaged", "at": null, "done": true, "current": false },
        { "status": "In Progress", "at": "2026-10-29 09:12:03.000000", "done": true, "current": false },
        { "status": "Resolved", "at": "2026-10-30 11:20:45.000000", "done": false, "current": true },
        { "status": "Closed", "at": null, "done": false, "current": false }
      ],
      "history": [
        { "status": "New", "at": "2026-10-28 15:41:40.112233" },
        { "status": "In Progress", "at": "2026-10-29 09:12:03.000000" },
        { "status": "Resolved", "at": "2026-10-30 11:20:45.000000" }
      ],
      "needs_confirmation": true,
      "ratings": { "rating_overall": null, "rating_quality": null, "rating_communication": null, "rating_response_time": null },
      "comments": [
        { "id": "a1b2c3d4e5", "text": "Please check again now.", "by": "Mohammed Ali", "mine": false, "at": "2026-10-30 11:21:00.000000" }
      ],
      "attachments": [
        { "name": "e890f3425b", "file_name": "stock_valuation_screenshot.png", "file_size": 70, "creation": "2026-10-28 15:41:45.380698" }
      ]
    }
  }
  ```

  **Response fields:**

  | Field | Type | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `module` | string / null | Module picked on Raise Ticket. Use this, not the `Module:` line in `description`. |
  | `project_title` | string / null | Project name for `project`. |
  | `raised_by` | string | Display name of the user who raised it. |
  | `created` | datetime | When the ticket was raised. Same key as in `get_tickets`. |
  | `resolution_notes` | string / null | Plain text, filled when the team resolves it. |
  | `assigned_to` | string[] | Display names (full name) of the team members working on it, e.g. `["Mohammed Ali"]`. `[]` = not assigned yet. |
  | `hours_logged`, `progress` | number / null | From the linked task. `null` until the ticket becomes a task. |
  | `steps[]` | `{status, at, done, current}` | The timeline. `status` is the ticket status, `done` = passed, `current` = where it is now. |
  | `history[]` | `{status, at}` | Only the status changes that really happened, oldest first. |
  | `ratings` | object | The client's 1–5 stars from `confirm_fix`, or `null` per rating if not given. |
  | `attachments[]` | `{name, file_name, file_size, creation}` | `name` is the File ID for **Open attachment**. `file_size` is in bytes. |

  **Errors:**

  - **401:** Token missing, expired or invalid. Refresh once and retry, else sign out.
  - **403:** Another client company's ticket, or a ticket raised by someone else (Client User), or role not allowed.
  - **404:** Ticket not found.

  **Notes:**

  - Timeline: `done` green check, `current` maroon ring, others grey.
  - A step can be `done: true` with `at: null`. The ticket skipped it (for example it went from New straight to In Progress, past Triaged), so there is no time to show. This is expected, not an error.
  - `needs_confirmation` true: show "It is fixed" and "Still an issue".
}
